## GLOBAL LORE CONSTRAINTS

These rules govern all event design. They are hard constraints.

| Rule | Statement |
|---|---|
| **Shardbearers** | NOT a faction. Origin: convicts → mercs → assassins → Calix Corp execs → Rift expedition → vanished. Now roaming anomaly individuals. No installations, no outposts, no political standing. Never appear as map actors. |
| **Shardbearer roster (866)** | Chaddy-O (disappeared 851), **Skrit Grimweave (active — Warrens, identity concealed)**, Smiling Nimbus (disappeared 851), Karim (out of closed beta scope), Oscar Calix/Oz (out of closed beta scope) |
| **Karim** | Deep-one hybrid. The only named Shardbearer Clayd personally fears. Referenced by name in Clayd's arc as absent threat only. Never appears as actor in closed beta. |
| **Skrit is a Shardbearer** | Identity concealed at 866. Hidden via `hidden_effect` in history file. No other character recognises him. Recognition fires when he obtains the Warrens duchy title. |
| **Bar massacre** | The figures who killed the Rooks are Shardbearers. Canonical design truth. Never stated in any in-game text within closed beta. |
| **Prince of Myr** | Fabricated propaganda title. No canonical ancient prince exists. Caelorin built it from forged/unverifiable documents. |
| **7th Legion** | Acts sovereign, denies sovereignty. Two named figures: **Corven Vultarre** (martial commander) and **Lyssa Varayne** (Nightglass Division, shadow intelligence). |
| **Vessels** | Collective entity — priest-general caste system. NOT a single ruler. |
| **Skarlmagicka** | Long-term corruption pressure on Skrit. Slow systemic destabilisation, not immediate death. |
| **Frozt / Ice Mandate** | Caliphate authority derives from Ice Mandate religious governance system. Caliph: **Marzuk Bin David**. |
| **New Cauldron** | Lireth Davan is **Senator** (NOT Senate-Primus). Technocratic republican representative. |
| **Clayd street language** | Never uses "Shardbearers". Uses: "those people", "the ones from the bar", "Karim's lot", "the problem", "thugs of a different calibre". |
| **Xerxes** | A planet, not a coastline. Aelthorin's elves are heirs to Xerxes the Hero of Myr's legacy from the First of the Third. |
| **Oscar Calix** | Governs Calix Corp via mortal clone. Oz (god form) exists separately. Neither encountered in closed beta. |
| **Shardbearer roaming events** | Out of scope for closed beta entirely. |

