> ```
> Followed by: `add_county_modifier = { modifier = eotg_nc_dejure_locked years = 20 }` on all flipped counties. Flag `eotg_legion_dejure_origin` must be set on all Legion de jure titles in history files. Does NOT fire if Legion retained independence as contracted partner.

**Win Condition 4 — The Unified Warrens** (`Skrit`)
Fires simultaneously with `eotg_skrit_recognition_001`. This IS the struggle-ending event. No choices for Skrit. `eotg_first_burrowlord` modifier applied. `eotg_identity_concealed` removed. `eotg_shardbearer_skrit` becomes visible to trigger checks.

**Win Condition 5 — The Ascendant Compact of Helix** (`Clayd`)
Closing event: **"FROM THE DRAINAGE DISTRICT."** Draws the explicit parallel — Helix Corp once backed Xerxes the Hero of Myr, a nobody who unified the Clusters against an empire. Helix was consumed by its own corporate logic and drowned with the city that bore his name. Clayd grew up in the drainage channels beneath those towers. He has made the same climb. Closes: *"Helix Corp is not what it was. It is what it was supposed to become."* `eotg_helix_ascendant` modifier applied.

**Win Condition 6 — The Frozt Dominion of Myr** (`Marzuk Bin David`)
Divine revelation event — Frozt's presence in conquered Clusters confirmed. Jihad declared fulfilled. Frozt Holy War CB options extended. All Cluster counties receive Froztam faith conversion pressure.

**Win Condition 7 — The Industrial Compact of Myr** (`Grezzik`)
Second Charter signing event. Rughan Broad-Jaw's engineering class receives formal governance representation. `eotg_second_charter` modifier applied. If ogre stakeholder arc completed: Rughan Broad-Jaw is named Co-Signatory.

**Win Condition 8 — The Principality of Myr** (`Caelorin`)
Closing event: **"THE MYTH THAT BECAME THE LAW."** The fabricated documents are now the founding instruments of an actual state. Every attending ruler at the ceremony knows the documents are suspect. None say so. The political cost of saying so is now higher than accepting them. `eotg_princes_peace` modifier applied. Claim fabrication strength reduced — he no longer needs it.

**Win Condition 9 — The Empire of Xerxes** (`Aelthorin`)
Closing event: **"WHAT XERXES WANTED."** Aelthorin does not call it victory. He calls it completion. Xerxes the Hero unified the Myr Clusters against an empire that wanted to erase them and died before he could govern what he built. The elves who survived on the planet that bears his name have spent three centuries and one catastrophic flood trying to be worthy of what he started. Closes with Xerxes the Hero's speech line: *"We stood together — and we prevailed."* Mechanics: Xerxes the planet becomes de jure capital of the Empire title. Aelthorin receives unique dynasty modifier linking his house to the Xerxes legacy. Water Oni vigilance doctrine becomes the Cluster's official cultural policy framework.

**Win Condition 10 — Empire of the Myr Clusters** (`Non-bookmark victor`)
Generic closing event: "THE CLUSTERS FIND THEIR CENTRE." Brief world-state flavor. No character-specific content. Standard `eotg_cluster_dominance` modifier.

